        "hydrology": null,
        "soils": "The parent is calcareous loess, the formed soil are Albi-Halic Luvisols wih 2,6-3,3% organic mater content and C/N ratio of 13,9 in the 0-10cm horizon (Szombathová and Zaujec, 2001, Gonet et al., 2008).",
        "vegetation": "The geobiocoenosis belongs to the Fageto-Quercetum group of forest type (Kubí?ek and Brechtl, 1970), with prevailing oaks- Quercus robur, Q. petraea, Q.cerris with admixtute of Carpinus betulus and Acer campestre in the tree layer of phytocoenosis. The herbaceous layer is dominated by Mellica uniflora, Dactylis glomerata, Carex pilosa, Asperula odorata, Hedera helix, Pulmonaria officinalis and Geum urbanum."
      },
